Subject: Keep PHP 7.4's pointers and capabilities intact under Fil-C
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

The PHP 7.4 counterpart of php-8.4-filc.patch, without the fiber and WeakMap
parts, which 7.4 does not have.

Fil-C traps on inline assembly it cannot prove safe. Take Zend's existing
portable paths for string comparison (memcmp) and zend_safe_address, and
spell xgetbv as the instruction Fil-C lowers instead of raw opcode bytes.

Fil-C also drops a pointer's capability when the pointer becomes an integer.
PHP 7.4's zend_type is a uintptr_t holding either a type code or a class
name or class entry pointer tagged in its low bits, and PHP trapped at
startup registering the first internal function with a class type. Make it
a char pointer under Fil-C, tagged with pointer arithmetic, as PHP 8's
zend_type keeps its pointer in a pointer. Typed-property references tag
their source list through the integer member of a union; make that member a
pointer too.

Fil-C checks that a function is called with the arguments it takes. php -m
called print_extension_info(), which takes two, through a one-argument
function pointer; give it one, as PHP 8 does.

zend_str_tolower_dup_ex(), zend_string_tolower_ex(), php_string_toupper()
and php_string_tolower() reached into the new copy as source pointer plus
(copy - source), which keeps the capability of the source. Offset the copy
instead.

--- a/Zend/zend_cpuinfo.c
+++ b/Zend/zend_cpuinfo.c
@@ -81,7 +81,7 @@ static unsigned get_xcr0_eax() {
 	// directly because older assemblers do not include support for xgetbv and
 	// there is no easy way to conditionally compile based on the assembler used.
 	unsigned eax, edx;
-	__asm__(".byte 0x0f, 0x01, 0xd0" : "=a"(eax), "=d"(edx) : "c"(0));
+	__asm__("xgetbv" : "=a"(eax), "=d"(edx) : "c"(0));
 	return eax;
 # elif defined(ZEND_WIN32) && defined(_XCR_XFEATURE_ENABLED_MASK)
 	return _xgetbv(_XCR_XFEATURE_ENABLED_MASK);
